{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-12-Mar-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 35, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "A gift in the form of a cube, whose side measures 10 cm, has to be wrapped with gift paper, which costs ₹0.05 per cm2. Find the cost of the gift wrap.", "options": [{"text": "₹60", "added": false}, {"text": "₹300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "₹30"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A and B together can do a piece of work in 13 days and A alone can do it in 18 days. In how many days can B alone do it?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A chair is listed at ₹600 and a discount of 8% is given. The selling price is:", "options": [{"text": "₹592", "added": false}, {"text": "₹584", "added": false}, {"text": "₹552", "added": false}, {"text": "₹600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "₹552"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A number when increased by 40 %', gives 3780. The number is:", "options": [{"text": "5400", "added": false}, {"text": "8100", "added": false}, {"text": "1350", "added": false}, {"text": "2700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "2700"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Find the value of", "options": [{"text": "7202", "added": false}, {"text": "7195", "added": false}, {"text": "7197", "added": false}, {"text": "7211", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "7202"}, {"n": 6, "text": "The sum of five numbers is 655. The average of the first two numbers is 75 and the third number is 123. Find the average of theremaining two numbers?", "options": [{"text": "191", "added": false}, {"text": "198", "added": false}, {"text": "199", "added": false}, {"text": "192", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "191"}, {"n": 7, "text": "Pipes A and B can fill an empty cistern in 13 minutes and 39 minutes, respectively. Both Pipe A and Pipe B are opened together. After how much time should Pipe A be turned off so that the empty cistern is completely filled in a total of 27 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "7 min", "added": false}, {"text": "10 min", "added": false}, {"text": "4 min", "added": false}, {"text": "5 min", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": "4 min"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The perimeter of a square is 14 cm. If each side of the square is increased by x cm, its area increases by 120 cm2. What is the value of x?", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "8"}, {"n": 9, "text": "After 58 litres of petrol was poured into an empty storage tank, it was still 1% empty. How much petrol (in litres, rounded off to two decimal place) must be poured into the storage tank in order to fill it?", "options": [{"text": "59.59", "added": false}, {"text": "57.59", "added": false}, {"text": "58.59", "added": false}, {"text": "59", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "fill-empty", "key_answer": "58.59"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two banks, A and B, offered loans at 3.5% and 6% per annum, respectively. Mukund borrowed an amount of ₹440000 from each bank. Find the positive difference between the amounts of simple interest paid to the two banks by Mukund after 4 years.", "options": [{"text": "43500", "added": false}, {"text": "44000", "added": false}, {"text": "45500", "added": false}, {"text": "45000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "44000"}, {"n": 11, "text": "The sum of five numbers is 655. The average of the first two numbers is 78 and the third number is 118. Find the average of the remaining two numbers?", "options": [{"text": "197", "added": false}, {"text": "190.5", "added": false}, {"text": "196", "added": false}, {"text": "191.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "190.5"}, {"n": 12, "text": "The amount that ₹4,375 computes in 2 years at annual compound interest, if the rates for the successive years be 8% and 12% per annum, respectively, is:", "options": [{"text": "₹4,417", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,292", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,812", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,250", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹5,292"}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "(9/5)^4"}, {"n": 14, "text": "There are 2822 students in a school and the ratio of boys to girls in the school is 36 : 47, then find the number of boys in school.", "options": [{"text": "1224", "added": false}, {"text": "1207", "added": false}, {"text": "1226", "added": false}, {"text": "1218", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "1224"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The difference between a discount of 30% on ₹2,200 and two successive discounts of 25% and 5% on the same amount is:", "opti